00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:09.590 align:start position:0%
 
Zardo  hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  and manga and today we're going to be  doing us a good old-fashioned ranking in  regards to parts one through eight of  JoJo's Bizarre Adventure and just a  warning before we hop into things this  is going to be a super subjective video  here in the criteria for how I'll be  ranking the various parts is how much I  personally enjoyed them and of course I  will do my best to explain why that was  or in fact why I didn't enjoy them  because we all know that's bound to come  up at least once so I guess I should say  to anyone who's new to the channel that  I am quite new to the judge of us myself  and at the moment these are all my  initial impressions meaning that this  ranking could very easily change upon  reflection later in life after having  spent more time digesting series it is  another fun thing  due to the extreme difference between  pots with radically shifting genres that  appeal to different people depending on  what it is they like it is highly  unlikely that my pot ranking will be the  same as yours  well perhaps anybody's so please do feel  free to share your individuality by  leaving your personal preferences in the  comments below but with that out of the  way let's begin welcome to an arbitrary  new world review ranking of every Jojo  pot number 8 phantom blood my feelings  regarding pot 1 have not changed one bit  with the greater context of everything  else in fact in comparison to every  other part phantom blood continues to be  lacking and I think I said this in my  initial thoughts on it but it's not a  bad story by any means especially  considering the time period that it was  made in how phantom blood is I guess  painfully standed there's nothing that  truly elevates it into a memorable  experience everything about it is just  kind of flat it features by far the most  boring Jojo in the story sorry Jonathan  but that is just your role in life who  has no real depth of character and  represents something of an octa as for  the villain do is admittedly much more  interesting with Jonathan but he is  still so pointlessly evil and not quite  cartoonish enough to fit the bill of  what I would call peak deer and as for  the genre I think that part 1 very much  fails as an action horror piece and the  primary power system involved in it  being come on was underwhelming and  uninteresting most of the time although  I should say that it would be far far  better implement it in part 2 and look  phantom blood is the reason why it took  me four tries to actually get into  JoJo's Bizarre Adventure it might only  be a handful of chapters and nine  episodes but it feels so sluggish and  pointless that the temptation to give up  is just too strong at least  statistically 75  of the time I do appreciate that it laid  down some much-needed story to give  other parts the richness of the world  they enjoy but on its own I honestly  never want to read or watch this part of  the story ever again  number seven stone ocean now while  there's only one ranking difference from  fountain blood I want to be clear stone  ocean is far far far and above it in  terms of almost literally every aspect  of storytelling it features a fun cast  with the Jojo that I quite enjoy and  some really intriguing stands as well as  a climactic conclusion the likes of  which still has yet to be equaled in the  franchise where stone Ocean loses me  quite a bit though is its setting which  is a stock standard boring prison  anything and I don't care how many  people say dude how are you supposed to  make a prison interesting because it can  be done and it has been done in a lot of  other series but the lack of an  interesting setting forces so much of  the narrative heavy lifting solely onto  the characters themselves and I do think  that they do their best it just lacks  that general support of the world and  that's not all though because stone  Ocean is just one of those things where  I really don't know how to feel about it  because at the eleventh hour we are  introduced to a universal restructuring  stand power that just puts a full stop  on the Jojo universe as we knew it and I  don't necessarily mind that at all in  fact I'm quite endlessly fascinated by  made in heaven but it's a rather grand  escalation that isn't in any way built  up to considering we spent about like  80% of the series fighting very minor  threats in a very cramped and boring  prison there were just a lot of things  that stone Ocean is missing pieces of  connective tissue that if in place could  have really made this one of the greater  Jojo parts in my opinion but it just  happened to fall a bit flat very sad  stuff number 6 Stardust Crusaders  now I feel like a lot of people are now  calling me a blasphemous heathen by  placing pot three so far down the list  but I would like to stop by saying that  Stardust Crusaders features what is  probably my favorite coal group of  characters because Joshua polnareff  Joseph kakuhen abdullah and the  magnificent iggy are all iconic in my  mind and having a series that does adopt  a pretty laid-back comical element with  their interactions was always good fun  to watch however and this is a big  however it just did not fit the tone of  what Stardust Crusaders was trying to do  as a set up this is the larger scale  Jojo story yet well we finally need to  deal with deal once and for all  this is quite literally a fate of the  world scenario at hand here and for most  of the part we spend  90% of our time getting caught in  seemingly unnecessary roadblocks like  fun arse ongoing battle with bathrooms  which while funny just felt like we were  moving so slowly and very rarely did  these encounters actually go on to serve  to develop any of our established  characters the formula was basically our  team arrived in whatever random town or  place they'd go to a stand user or to is  conveniently waiting for them there one  of the group notices something weird and  really really frustrating Lee decides  for no good reason never to tell anyone  about it  at which point shenanigan rien sues the  stand user is beaten and our characters  returned to the status quo to repeat  their mistakes all over again  never learning anything and there are of  course some exceptions to this but they  are more the exception that proves the  rule because that's how the majority of  the series felt to me and it's not so  bad when you finally come to the  understanding that you just need to sit  back and enjoy what plays out in front  of you rather than actively searching  for some kind of story or character  development and it does have one hell of  an ending with the final two battles  against Vanilla Ice and deer hitting  those feels really really hard so there  is plenty to love about Stardust  Crusaders I just feel like most of the  other parts took this formula and  implemented it a hell of a lot better  number five  Jojo Lian next up is the most recent  addition to the series and the only part  that is as of yet incomplete so it's  ranking here is not fair at all because  depending on how things conclude it  could quite easily rise or it could  quite easily fall but thus far Jojo Lian  has been a really fun journey that takes  full advantage of the entire heritage of  JoJo's Bizarre Adventure constructing an  intriguing alternate Joestar family tree  as well as bringing in some other  classically known names back into the  fray like one Yoshioka kira for example  and what Jojo Lian has going strongly  for it though is that it features  probably the most intriguing Jojo we've  ever had in my opinion and I do very  much enjoy the journey we're going on to  find out both who he used to be as well  as watch him discover who he is now and  when I put it like that yeah it does  sound like a bit of a wanker journey of  self-discovery but that is kind of what  it is and it does work very well within  the greater genre of mystery each of the  secondary characters are also  fascinating in their own right as well  except for you and overall part 8 just  feels so strong the only thing I could  really criticize it for is often feeling  like it lacks direction but at the same  time that's exactly what a mystery is  you don't get to know the destination  before you get there and as a result you  are forced to just sit back and enjoy  yourself which I very much did with Jojo  Leon  number four golden wind so here we have  a true jojo triumph golden wind is one  of those examples of taking the stardust  crusaders formula and perfecting it  making it feel like our characters were  making great amounts of progress while  simultaneously still keeping the stand  of the weak structure in addition to  that golden wind features an incredibly  solid group of protagonists with a  fantastic sense of brotherhood that  develops around them through all the  experiences they come to be subject to  and I'll single out booty arathi and  Mistah in particular as characters who  captivated me throughout golden wind but  what really impressed me was just how  fantastically Italy was used as a  backdrop for the story the dedication to  detail and the construction of every  frame is at the very least worthy of  being called a pure work of art and I  loved that the designs of each character  also reflect the nature of this ornate  and stunning landscape because the  costumes in particular of golden wind  are unique even for a jojo series and it  was a really cool change of aesthetic  the one detractor I do have is that I  felt like Jonah was one of the more  boring JoJo's who was constantly being  out shown by I don't know literally  every one and I got a lot of feedback in  my golden wind review stating that  Jonah's character arc is just a lot more  subtle than others and while I  appreciate that and I do take the  arguments you all made that still does  not make him interesting or believable  to me I'd still insist that he is a 15  year old deus ex machina who will make  the perfect choice in any given scenario  99% of the time yes he does make  mistakes those mistakes are another  exception that proves the rule and in  some cases those mistakes end up being  the best cause of action anyway so what  I will give Jonah is that he was cool as  was golden experience Requiem and the  whole idea of requiems in general which  I feel is criminally under explored in  the series going forward but what can  you do I guess  number three battle tendency in terms of  story alone I would call this the best  church apart by far battle tendency  exists in a priest ant world where our  key wasn't capable of just doing the  weekly villain thingy  and that actually forced him to  construct a story of what he know a  story which was fantastic and I really  wish that he would do that a lot more  because part two shows that he is  perfectly capable of doing sir even at  that early stage of the series battle  tendency also very effectively fixed the  issues I had with phantom blood because  you know how Jojo is now actually  interesting heavily flawed of course and  in need of some learning as well as  character growth but that's the great  part and the side characters were  equally as compelling in the  antagonists of The Pillowman what an  improvement on dear or at least mama was  cause was very generically evil as was  ac/dc and Santana I don't even remember  few had a personality at all but wamu is  the key here and I still find it insane  that some people despise Part two as  much as they do and the last time I said  this none of you stayed at the battle  tendency is like universally loved but  from everything I've experienced no it  most certainly is not  I've seen people call this by far the  worst part in giorgo and I'm just like  are you out of your mind  and actually you know what if you want  one of those people please please do  leave a comment explaining what you  don't like about battle tenancy because  I am legitimately curious but for now  part two is easily one of my fondest  memories of this entire saga number two  diamond is unbreakable so things just  don't get much more perfect than part  four because this is the sweet spot of  Jojo this is the part where everything  just makes sense and fits into place all  thanks to a very simple genre change  choosing to leave the realm of  action-adventure and adopting a slice of  life format and it's difficult to  express just how much this enhances our  key storytelling because the chilled  nature of part 4 allows all of the  smallest subtle details to shine like  taking the time to properly enjoy what  may have been considered almost to fill  a story in part 3 but here everything's  just a lot of fun and a lot of that  might be because the stakes aren't  incredibly high here even after the main  antagonist is introduced because in the  end he's just a serial killer Kira is  not some world ending superpower and  that also goes on to make him one of the  greatest villains in the series because  this guy just wants to live a quiet life  and keeps incremental e needing to  escalate his actions to do so which was  really fascinating to watch but the  slice of life genre also helps the  entire ensemble of part 4 because it  allows them to stay in the picture  rather than being defeated and then just  never showing up again which gives us  gems like Rohan and a crazy amount of  time to explore him and others as well  as providing an opportunity to explore  some of the weirdest and powers as well  which aren't necessarily designed for  pure combat because combat is not  necessarily the name of the game in part  4 and yeah Dimond is unbreakable just  has it all and it is in my opinion the  crowning achievement of the first church  of us however we still have yet to  examine number one  steel ball run so if part four was  changing the genre to suit our keys  favored model then part seven is what  happens when our key properly adapts his  model to the more standard Church of  action-adventure realm and the result is  what I would consider to easily be the  greatest part in the series steel ball  run in many ways benefits from being  allowed to be its own thing without  having to be tethered to all of the  established Jojo history and stuff and  so we can do things like you know enter  a horse race and search for the corpse  of Christ  whilst being pursued relentlessly by the  President of the United States of  America but still bull run stepped up  the Joe Joe game in every conceivable  way firstly by presenting an incredibly  unique setting as well as a clear goal  that we needed to work towards in  regards to winning the race but it was  like looking at the peak of the mountain  from sea level and through this  structure our key was able to very  smoothly implement stand battles that in  no way to track from the end goal or  from the characters who wielded them and  that remains easily my favorite aspect  of steel ball run in fact that stands  are a utility a side story really and  the main focus is always on the  characters very well written characters  as well with gyro zeppeli being a clear  standout but not too far ahead of an  impressively morally ambiguous Johnny  Joestar a very conflicting alternate  dear and mister Stars and Stripes  himself everything about steel ball run  just works and I would definitely call  it our keys magnum opus because as much  as I love aspects of every other part  steel ball run is lightning in a bottle  it's an incredibly rare find and I  greatly appreciate having gotten to read  it and as such it is definitely my  favorite part of JoJo's Bizarre  Adventure and that pretty much does it  for my ranking of parts one through  eight of JoJo's Bizarre Adventure if you  enjoyed this video and the content this  channel produce in general then please  do consider donating to the new  worldview patreon because the support of  all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  plot this channel and incredible amount  and if you'd like to join the fun at any  time then please do head over to my  disco server where a wide array of  Shannara takes place on a daily basis  and finally please do comment with your  own personal charger apart rankings this  has been the new old review and I'll see  you next time  [Music]

